In article <haber.668589102@acf9> haber@acf9.nyu.edu (eli haber) writes:
[] Can somebody out there tell me why people seem to like playing as
[] a wizard?

_I_ like playing a wizard character because:

1) you start with a blessed +1 athame (of 'Elbereth' engraving),
    aka Ghostbuster.

2) you start with a cloak of magic resistance which prevents many
    surprise traps from catching you with your pants down, so to speak.

3) the wizard character isn't a barbarian, it has to think its way
    thru the early game (when things are most fun).

4) there's the possibility that you start with some def' magic (word up!).
    even seemingly useless items can be very useful at times.

personally, i adopted wizards way back in Hack 1.02 (Intro to NetHack) ...

btw, wizards cannot intrinsically identify items or recognize curses,
however priests can.  priests are also highly recommended (and not
just for beginners).

